cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or coursework, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "Explainable Hybrid Deep Learning-Based Network Intrusion Detection System"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
url: "https://github.com/norriy0u/Explainable-Hybrid-Deep-Learning-IDS"
repository-code: "https://github.com/norriy0u/Explainable-Hybrid-Deep-Learning-IDS"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A collaborative third-year undergraduate engineering project implementing an explainable
  network intrusion detection system (IDS) using a hybrid deep learning architecture.
  Combines 1D-CNN, Bidirectional LSTM, and trainable temporal attention with SHAP
  (SHapley Additive exPlanations) for 10-class multiclass attack classification on the
  UNSW-NB15 benchmark dataset. Deployed via an interactive Streamlit SOC-style dashboard.
  Developed as part of a Deep Learning elective (Fifth Semester).
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - cybersecurity
  - deep learning
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - CNN
  - BiLSTM
  - attention mechanism
  - network security
  - UNSW-NB15
  - PyTorch
  - Keras
  - Streamlit
